---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { firm } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Anveshana Advocates & Consultants handles information collected through this website."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lines={['Privacy']}
  lead="What this website collects, what it does not, and how enquiries are handled."
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not run advertising trackers, does not set analytics
    cookies, does not collect anything through a form, and does not build a
    profile of you. It is a set of static pages.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Enquiries</h3>
  <p>
    There is no enquiry form on this website. When you use one of the
    &ldquo;request a consultation&rdquo; buttons, your browser opens WhatsApp
    with a message ready to send to the chambers. Nothing is submitted to this
    website, and we receive nothing at all unless you choose to press send in
    WhatsApp.
  </p>
  <p>
    Whatever you then send us — your name, your number and what you tell us
    about your matter — we use solely to respond to you and, if you become a
    client, to act on the matter. We do not sell it, rent it, or share it for
    marketing. WhatsApp messages are carried by WhatsApp, and Meta's own
    privacy terms apply to that service. If you would rather not use it, call
    or email the chambers instead.
  </p>

  <h3>Local storage</h3>
  <p>
    Your browser stores two small values on your own device: a record that you
    have acknowledged the disclaimer, so you are not asked again on every
    visit, and a note that you have already seen the opening animation in this
    browsing session. Neither is a tracking cookie, neither identifies you,
    and neither is transmitted to us or to anyone else. Clearing your browser
    data removes both.
  </p>

  <h3>Server logs</h3>
  <p>
    Like any website, this site is served by a hosting provider that records
    standard technical request logs, which may include IP address, browser
    type and the page requested. These are retained by the provider for
    security and operational purposes.
  </p>

  <h3>Maps</h3>
  <p>
    The map on the contact page does not load until you click to load it. If
    you choose to load it, Google receives a request from your browser and its
    own privacy policy applies from that point. If you never click, no request
    is made.
  </p>

  <h2>Confidentiality and privilege</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Please do not send confidential, sensitive or privileged material — by
      WhatsApp, by email or otherwise — before we have confirmed an
      engagement.
    </strong>
    Information sent to us before an advocate–client relationship exists may
    not attract privilege, however it was transmitted.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once we act for you, everything you tell us is governed by our
    professional duty of confidentiality, which is considerably stricter than
    anything described on this page and continues after the matter ends.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries that do not become matters are retained only for as long as
    needed to deal with them and to run conflict checks. Client files are
    retained for the period required by our professional and statutory
    obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You may ask us what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it,
    or ask us to delete an enquiry that has not become a matter. Write to

    <a href={`mailto:${firm.email}`}>{firm.email}</a> and we will respond.
    Requests relating to an active or former client file are subject to our
    professional record-keeping obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this notice changes, the revised version will be published on this page
    with a new date below.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {firm.legalName}, {firm.address.line1}, {firm.address.line2},
    {firm.address.city} {firm.address.postalCode}.
    <br />
    <a href={`mailto:${firm.email}`}>{firm.email}</a> ·
    <a href={`tel:${firm.phoneHref}`}>{firm.phone}</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
